<title>ARGENTINA: TABLE-Banco Frances Q4 net shr US$0.21.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Banco Frances Q4 net shr US$0.21.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>In thousands of US$ except income per share, income per</p>
<p>ADS and percentages</p>
<p>		30/6/1997   31/3/97  30/6/96   31/3/97   30/6/96</p>
<p>Net Financial</p>
<p>   Income    72,622     52,699    52,188    37.81%     39.15%</p>
<p>Provision for</p>
<p>loan losses</p>
<p>		(8,300)   (11,211)  (11,230)  (25.97%)   (26.09%)</p>
<p>Net income</p>
<p>from services</p>
<p>		 36,853     30,250    31,558    21.83%     16.78%</p>
<p>Administrative</p>
<p>expenses</p>
<p>	     (55,055)   (48,472)  (46,259)    13.58%     19.01%</p>
<p>Income from</p>
<p>equity</p>
<p>investments</p>
<p>		  3,285	2,939     2,461    11.77%     33.48%</p>
<p>Inflation</p>
<p>Adjustment</p>
<p>		(1,006)    (1,847)     (264)  (45.53%)    281.06%</p>
<p> Other	(7,640)	6,393	 262 (219.51%) (3016.03%)</p>
<p>Income tax</p>
<p>		(9,186)    (9,806)   (6,064)   (6.32%)     51.48%</p>
<p>Net income</p>
<p>for the</p>
<p>   period    31,573     20,945    22,652    50.74%     39.38%</p>
<p>Net income</p>
<p>per share (B)</p>
<p>		   0.21	 0.14	0.15    50.74%     39.38%</p>
<p>Net income</p>
<p>per ADS (C)</p>
<p>		   0.64	 0.43	0.46    50.74%     39.38%</p>
<p>(A) Exchange rate: 1 Ps. = 1 US$</p>
<p>(B) Assumes 147.457.460 ordinary shares outstanding in each period.</p>
<p>(C) Each ADS represents three ordinary shares.</p>
<p>The increase in Net Income versus the quarter ended March 31, 1997  and the quarter ended June 30, 1996, was mainly related to an increase  in Net financial income and Net income from services and lower Provision  for loan losses, partly offset by an increase in Administrative expenses  and a loss recorded in Other income.</p>
